WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.930
So one of the things about-- remarkable things about science is, usually no model is 

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:09.480
completely correct. Because of 

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:10.860
biology and evolution,

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:13.920
organisms do the most amazing, crazy things,

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:16.140
and so they almost can make any model work.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.650
There will be an organism out there that will fit a model.

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:23.920
And so there is now some recent evidence where environment can effect the 

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:24.500
progeny.

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:29.640
An example would be the recent discovery of a novel 

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:31.000
bacterial immune system,

00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:36.230
where bacteria that are exposed to a 

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:40.660
virus take a piece of that virus and put it into its 

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:45.710
own chromosomes, as a then heritable marker that they 

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:47.000
have been in their past,

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:51.550
exposed to that virus, such that when the 

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:56.450
progeny of those parental cells that were exposed to the virus, 

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:59.290
are then exposed to the virus,

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:01.660
they're going to be resistant to it.

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:05.440
And so there is a case where environment is changing the genetic material,

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:07.480
which is then being propagated on.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:09.160
It's an exception,

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:10.030
so it doesn't say that,

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:10.300
you know,

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:13.330
but it's certainly not the driving force for most of evolution,

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:14.850
as Lamarck postulated it.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:20.150
But there are examples now coming up where the genetic material somehow does respond to 

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:24.950
environment and adapts itself to maybe make the progeny more fit, 

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:26.150
in that sense.

